The prior triage is not the right native construction: arbitrary added arcs would leave the paper’s product class. The paper instead gives a much cleaner native route. Lemmas 4.3–4.5 force a unique cycle-cover program along cosets of \((1,-1)\), and equation (4.13) reduces “one cycle” to an exact gcd check. Proposition 1.1 also makes Track A impossible—the paper explicitly says its CRT/gcd test handles 100,000-digit inputs in seconds—so any viable build must be honest Track B.
